## Active recovery blocker

The GitHub connector can create files, blobs, trees, and commits, but it has no operation that applies a patch or uploads extracted local files as blob content. Several reconstructed blob objects are not present in the remote repository object database, so a connector-only tree commit cannot reference them. The agent container also cannot resolve `github.com`, preventing an authenticated local push.

The exported materialized tree is complete and compiled. Finishing the direct-source commit requires one authorized transfer mechanism for those file bytes. No additional encoded checkpoint has been created or pushed.

